│ fetal neck, irrespective of whether it is septated or not and whether it is confined to the neck or envelopes the    │
│ whole fetus. During the second trimester, the translucency usually resolves and, in a few cases, it evolves into     │
│ either nuchal edema or cystic hygromas with or without generalized hydrops. Increased NT is associated with trisomy  │
│ 21, Turner syndrome and other chromosomal defects as well as many fetal malformations and genetic syndromes. The     │
│ incidence of these abnormalities is related to the thickness, rather than the appearance, of NT The ability to       │
│ achieve a reliable measurement of NT is dependent on appropriate training and adherence to a standard technique in   │
