IVF cases. In twin pregnancies, the only significant difference was a 12% (95% CI: −34%–−3%) reduction in NT in IVF 
cases. In singleton pregnancies, the false‐positive rate for Down syndrome screening was 1.4% and 1.9% greater for the 
IVF and ICSI groups, respectively, compared to controls for a general screening population.   Conclusions Patients 
