| 273 | Combined first‐ and second‐trimester screening for Down syndrome: an evaluation of proMBP as a marker |         
Evaluates screening performance of different combinations of first- and second-trimester markers, including integrated  
tests |                                                                                                                 
| 288 | Combining first and second trimester markers for Down syndrome screening: think twice | Compares different      
screening strategies including integrated and serum integrated screening, which combine serum markers from both         
trimesters |                                                                                                            
| 292 | Second and first trimester estimation of risk for Down syndrome: implementation and performance in the SAFER    
study | Evaluates implementation and performance of integrated screening protocols (five- and six-marker) which combine 
first and second trimester serum markers |                                                                              
                                                                                                                        
**Excluded Studies (93):**                                                                                              
All other studies were excluded because they did not meet the core requirement of combining serum markers from BOTH     
trimesters. Common reasons for exclusion include:                                                                       
- First trimester serum screening only (e.g., studies 201, 206, 213, 215, 216, 250, 255, 261, 272, 275, 282, 286, 295)  
- Second trimester serum screening only (e.g., studies 202, 204, 207, 209, 221, 223, 224, 231, 239, 241, 243, 245, 247, 
251, 254, 268, 269, 270, 271, 276, 281, 284, 285, 300)                                                                  
- Ultrasound-only or ultrasound + single trimester serum (e.g., studies 203, 212, 214, 217, 218, 219, 220, 222, 226,    
