│ positive result in last pregnancy", "abstract": "Maternal serum screening for Down syndrome is a common practice in  │
│ the United Kingdom. A number of factors have been shown to influence the chance of a false positive test result.     │
│ Analysis of routinely collated information stored on an electronic database in a district general hospital has shown │
│ that women with a previous false positive maternal screen are at much greater chance of having a false positive      │
│ result in their next pregnancy. Overall, there was a fivefold increased risk attributed to biological variation in   │
│ their serum concentrations of alpha-feto protein (AFP) and human chorionic gonadotrophin (hCG). The potential effect │
