│ "Fifty‐six cases of Down syndrome were identified in a population of women who had undergone maternal serum triple   │
│ marker screening [alpha‐fetoprotein (AFP), human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG), and unconjugated oestriol (uE3)       │
│ analyses]. These affected pregnancies represented all known cases present in the population of 34 368 women          │
│ screened. Using a 1:270 mid‐trimester Down syndrome risk to define the screen‐positive group, 42 affected            │
